# Scope: Finance Doc Summarizer

Working doc. Keep it in the repo. It shows how you plan and make trade-offs.

## Goal

Upload a PDF. Get a structured, page-referenced summary in under a minute.

## Why this project

- Shows LLM API use, prompt design and structured output.
- Solves a real analyst task: reading long documents fast.
- Targets finance, compliance and BA roles.

## Target user

A business or financial analyst who must skim a long PDF (policy, annual report, regulatory notice, vendor contract) and extract what matters.

## In scope (MVP)

- Upload one text-based PDF (up to ~50 pages).
- Extract text page by page, keeping page numbers.
- Send text to an LLM with a fixed prompt.
- Return **structured JSON**, validated against a schema.
- Show the result in a simple web UI (Streamlit).
- Download the result as JSON and Markdown.
- Run from the command line too: `python summarize.py file.pdf`.

## Out of scope (for now)

- Scanned PDFs and OCR
- Multiple documents at once
- User accounts, databases, login
- Chat or follow-up questions (that's Project 2, the RAG chatbot)
- Fine-tuning or training any model

## Output schema

| Field | Type | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| `title` | string | Document title |
| `doc_type` | string | Policy, report, contract, notice, other |
| `one_line_summary` | string | Max 25 words |
| `executive_summary` | string | 3 to 5 sentences |
| `key_points` | list | Each with a `page` reference |
| `key_figures` | list | `label`, `value`, `page` |
| `risks_or_obligations` | list | Each with a `page` reference |
| `action_items` | list | Who, what, deadline if stated |
| `open_questions` | list | What the document leaves unclear |

Rule: if the document doesn't say it, the model must return an empty list. No guessing.

## Tech stack

| Layer | Choice | Why |
|-------|--------|-----|
| Language | Python 3.11+ | Standard for LLM work |
| PDF text | `pdfplumber` (or `pypdf`) | Simple, page-aware |
| LLM | Claude API via `anthropic` SDK | Model name set in `.env`, easy to swap |
| Validation | `pydantic` | Enforces the schema |
| UI | Streamlit | Fast, free hosting on Hugging Face Spaces |
| Tests | `pytest` | A few basic tests |

